# 80. Blast Radius, Budgets, Circuit Breakers and Autonomous-Operations Stop

Autonomy must be bounded not only by permission but also by impact.

## 80.1 Blast-Radius Limits

Policy may limit:

- Number of resources changed per action
- Number of Agents changed per window
- Percentage of sources disabled
- Number of external integrations activated
- Maximum configuration delta
- Number of retries
- Tool-chain depth
- Concurrent mutations

Artemis must not split one prohibited large change into many small changes to
circumvent a blast-radius limit.

## 80.2 Cost and Consumption Budgets

Autonomous research and operations should have bounded:

- External API spend
- LLM spend
- Token budget
- Network-request count
- Provider quota consumption
- Compute usage
- Storage growth
- Retry count
- Workflow duration

Exceeding a budget should stop or downgrade the workflow according to policy.

## 80.3 Circuit Breakers

Autonomous mutation should stop when material anomalies are detected, such as:

- Unexpected failure rate
- Verification mismatch
- Repeated rollback
- Unknown resource state
- Provider behavioral change
- Audit failure
- Policy-system failure
- Duplicate execution
- Excessive cost
- Repeated malformed tool output
- Cross-resource inconsistency

## 80.4 Artemis Operations Kill Switch

TitanGold should have an **Artemis Autonomous Operations Kill Switch** or
equivalent central control for operational writes.

When active:

- Autonomous write capability is disabled
- In-progress writes are stopped at the next safe boundary where possible
- New write capability leases are denied
- Read-only diagnosis may remain available if safe
- Trading Emergency Stop semantics remain separate and unchanged

This control must not be implemented only inside the LLM prompt.

Artemis must not clear its own Operations Kill Switch autonomously.

## 80.5 Safe Recovery Mode

After a circuit breaker or operations stop, Artemis may enter read-only recovery
analysis.

It may:

- Inspect state
- Identify incomplete operations
- Prepare rollback or recovery plans
- Report impact

Actual privileged recovery remains subject to the applicable authorization
class.

